1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,740
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:25,041
It's almost ten o'clock.

3
00:00:25,041 --> 00:00:28,178
I've got to go. Tomorrow is Monday,

4
00:00:28,178 --> 00:00:30,388
and work begins at eight in the morning for me.

5
00:00:30,388 --> 00:00:32,188
Oh, I'm so happy that Max is home.

6
00:00:32,188 --> 00:00:34,531
He's the sweetest little thing.

7
00:00:34,531 --> 00:00:36,278
I'll drive you to the station, dear.

8
00:00:36,278 --> 00:00:39,851
You can catch the ten-twenty train to Grand Central Station.

9
00:00:39,851 --> 00:00:41,803
I'll drive Susan, dear.

10
00:00:41,803 --> 00:00:43,077
Thank you, Philip.

11
00:00:43,077 --> 00:00:44,298
Then Grandpa, Robbie,

12
00:00:44,298 --> 00:01:02,762
and I can finish wrapping all these gifts.

13
00:01:02,762 --> 00:01:06,327
It's so good to have you home again ...

14
00:01:06,327 --> 00:01:12,164
and to see Max asleep in his bassinet at home with us.

15
00:01:12,164 --> 00:01:17,992
To be with our family and all that Stewart TLC.

16
00:01:17,992 --> 00:01:24,185
TLC--tender loving care.

17
00:01:24,185 --> 00:01:27,411
That's our motto.

18
00:01:27,411 --> 00:01:28,391
Did you see the washcloth

19
00:01:28,391 --> 00:01:31,323
and the towels with the teddy bears on them?

20
00:01:31,323 --> 00:01:34,496
Alexandra and the Molinas sent them for Max.

21
00:01:34,496 --> 00:01:36,946
It was so kind of them.

22
00:01:36,946 --> 00:01:38,987
Now Max has come into everyone's life.

23
00:01:38,987 --> 00:01:42,222
The house is so alive with him here.

24
00:01:42,222 --> 00:01:45,305
The welcome sign over the door.

25
00:01:45,305 --> 00:01:47,622
The boxes of presents.

26
00:01:47,622 --> 00:01:49,823
The M-A-X over his bassinet.

27
00:01:49,823 --> 00:01:52,381
Robbie put that there.

28
00:01:52,381 --> 00:01:54,047
Susan's teddy bear.

29
00:01:54,047 --> 00:02:00,882
So cuddly. The beautiful crib from Mom and Dad.

30
00:02:00,882 --> 00:02:05,017
Oh, and Grandpa's baseball glove.

31
00:02:05,017 --> 00:02:07,414
You know, it hung over my crib, too.

32
00:02:07,414 --> 00:02:09,784
And it hung over Robbie's crib.

33
00:02:09,784 --> 00:02:11,299
Part of Grandpa's magic?

34
00:02:11,299 --> 00:02:12,966
Oh, that's not all.

35
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,516
It hung over Susan's crib.

36
00:02:14,516 --> 00:02:15,800
The same baseball glove?

37
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:20,077
That's right. Grandpa hangs it there for good luck.

38
00:02:20,077 --> 00:02:24,426
He says it always brought him good luck on the baseball team.

39
00:02:24,426 --> 00:02:28,088
He believes it'll bring good luck to all the Stewart babies.

40
00:02:28,088 --> 00:02:29,274
And then he takes it back

41
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:29,969
when Max is ready to use it?

42
00:02:29,969 --> 00:02:30,895
Yes,

43
00:02:30,895 --> 00:02:32,624
and replaces it with a new glove

44
00:02:32,624 --> 00:02:34,469
so the old one will be ready

45
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:37,668
for a new member of the Stewart family.

46
00:02:37,668 --> 00:02:42,614
Grandpa really loves his family, doesn't he?

47
00:02:42,614 --> 00:02:45,082
So do I.

48
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:51,801
And so do I.

49
00:02:51,801 --> 00:02:53,744
And so does Max.

50
00:02:53,744 --> 00:02:53,744
After he eats!
